IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part1-preliminary`

-- scja1-part3-div3-sicc.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- LAYER 1, Part 3, Division 3 "Singapore International Commercial Court", ss 18A to 18M (s 18E is shown repealed). The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` and this part's s 2 module (for "Supreme Court Judge"). The Singapore International Commercial Court is its own `Court`
-- constructor in the core: whether the Act's "General Division" includes it is fork K1 of the keel, recorded at each site that turns on it.
-- A condition the Rules of Court set ("such conditions as the Rules of Court may prescribe") is a plain input: the Rules are not among the sources.

§ `Part 3: General Division of High Court (continued)`

§§ `Division 3: Singapore International Commercial Court`

§§§ `Section 18A: Singapore International Commercial Court`

-- Plain gloss: is this court the division of the General Division known as the Singapore International Commercial Court? "There shall be" such a division: it names no other.
-- src:1317 | 18A. There shall be a division of the General Division known as the
-- src:1318 | Singapore International Commercial Court.
@ref s 18A (src:1317-1318)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A the court is the division of the General Division known as the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section creates the division and does not say what else is or is not a division of the General Division

§§§ `Section 18B: President of Singapore International Commercial Court`

-- s 18B(1). Plain gloss: may the Chief Justice appoint this Judge to be the President of the SICC? A Supreme Court Judge, a Senior Judge or an International Judge: the grant names its complement,
-- so a Judicial Commissioner is outside it (NOTHING).
-- src:1324 | 18B.—(1) The Chief Justice may appoint a Supreme Court Judge, a
-- src:1325 | Senior Judge or an International Judge to be the President of the
-- src:1326 | Singapore International Commercial Court for such period as the
-- src:1327 | Chief Justice may specify.
@ref s 18B(1) (src:1324-1327)
GIVEN j IS A Judge
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18B(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` j EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF j's office EQUALS `Senior Judge` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF j's office EQUALS `International Judge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a Supreme Court Judge, a Senior Judge or an International Judge"

-- s 18B(2). If no appointment is made under (1), the Chief Justice is the President. "If" not met (an appointment was made) is a no for this subsection.
-- src:1331 | (2) If no appointment is made under subsection (1), the Chief
-- src:1332 | Justice is the President of the Singapore International Commercial
-- src:1333 | Court.
@ref s 18B(2) (src:1331-1333)
GIVEN `an appointment has been made under section 18B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Chief Justice appointed a President of the Singapore International Commercial Court under section 18B(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18B(2) the Chief Justice is the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an appointment has been made under section 18B(1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no appointment is made under subsection (1)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§§ `Section 18C: Act to apply with modifications`

-- Plain gloss: does this provision of the Act apply to proceedings in the SICC as it applies to proceedings in the General Division exercising its original civil jurisdiction?
-- "Subject to sections 18D to 18M and 80(2A)": where one of those modifies the provision, which of the two governs is for that section, so the answer is NOTHING here.
-- src:1344 | 18C. Subject to sections 18D to 18M and 80(2A), the provisions of
-- src:1345 | this Act apply to proceedings in the Singapore International
-- src:1346 | Commercial Court as they apply to proceedings in the General
-- src:1347 | Division exercising its original civil jurisdiction.
@ref s 18C (src:1344-1347)
GIVEN `sections 18D to 18M or 80(2A) modify the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any of sections 18D to 18M or 80(2A) modify the provision for proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18C the provision of the Act applies to proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court as to the General Division in its original civil jurisdiction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sections 18D to 18M or 80(2A) modify the provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to sections 18D to 18M and 80(2A)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§§ `Section 18D: Jurisdiction of Singapore International Commercial Court`

-- s 18D(1). Plain gloss: does the SICC have jurisdiction to hear and try this action? It must satisfy ALL of (a) international and commercial in nature; (b) one the General Division may hear and try in its
-- original civil jurisdiction; (c) such other conditions as the Rules of Court may prescribe.
-- src:1353 | 18D.—(1) The Singapore International Commercial Court has
-- src:1354 | jurisdiction to hear and try any action that satisfies all of the
-- src:1355 | following conditions:
-- src:1357 | (a) the action is international and commercial in nature;
-- src:1359 | (b) the action is one that the General Division may hear and try
-- src:1360 | in its original civil jurisdiction;
-- src:1362 | (c) the action satisfies such other conditions as the Rules of
-- src:1363 | Court may prescribe.
@ref s 18D(1) (src:1353-1363)
GIVEN `the action is international and commercial in nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action international and commercial in nature?
      `the General Division may hear and try the action in its original civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an action the General Division may hear and try in its original civil jurisdiction?
      `the action satisfies the other conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the action satisfy the other conditions the Rules of Court prescribe for the Singapore International Commercial Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear and try the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is international and commercial in nature`
           AND `the General Division may hear and try the action in its original civil jurisdiction`
           AND `the action satisfies the other conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any action that satisfies all of the following conditions"

-- s 18D(2)(a). Without limiting (1), jurisdiction to hear proceedings relating to international commercial arbitration that the General Division may hear and that satisfy the Rules' conditions.
-- src:1367 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Singapore International
-- src:1368 | Commercial Court (being a division of the General Division) has
-- src:1369 | jurisdiction —
-- src:1371 | (a) to hear any proceedings relating to international
-- src:1372 | commercial arbitration that the General Division may
-- src:1373 | hear and that satisfy such conditions as the Rules of Court
-- src:1374 | may prescribe;
@ref s 18D(2)(a) (src:1367-1374)
GIVEN `the proceedings relate to international commercial arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the proceedings relate to international commercial arbitration?
      `the General Division may hear the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they proceedings the General Division may hear?
      `the proceedings satisfy the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they satisfy the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(2)(a) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the proceedings relating to international commercial arbitration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings relate to international commercial arbitration` AND `the General Division may hear the proceedings` AND `the proceedings satisfy the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting subsection (1)": other routes remain; this paragraph names proceedings "that the General Division may hear and that satisfy such conditions"

-- s 18D(2)(b). Jurisdiction to hear an application (i) seeking relief for the purposes of proceedings in the SICC, (ii) made before those proceedings commence, (iii) satisfying the Rules' conditions.
-- src:1378 | (b) to hear any application —
-- src:1380 | (i) that seeks relief for the purposes of proceedings in
-- src:1381 | the Singapore International Commercial Court;
-- src:1383 | (ii) that is made before the commencement of such
-- src:1384 | proceedings; and
-- src:1386 | (iii) that satisfies such conditions as the Rules of Court
-- src:1387 | may prescribe; and
@ref s 18D(2)(b) (src:1378-1387)
GIVEN `the application seeks relief for the purposes of proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application seek relief for the purposes of proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court?
      `the application is made before the commencement of such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made before the proceedings have commenced?
      `the application satisfies the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application satisfy the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(2)(b) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application seeks relief for the purposes of proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court`
           AND `the application is made before the commencement of such proceedings`
           AND `the application satisfies the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting subsection (1)": other routes remain

-- s 18D(2)(c). Jurisdiction to hear proceedings relating to corporate insolvency, restructuring or dissolution under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or the Companies Act 1967 as in force
-- immediately before 30 July 2020, that are (i) international and commercial in nature and (ii) satisfy the Rules' conditions.
-- src:1391 | (c) to hear any proceedings relating to corporate insolvency,
-- src:1392 | restructuring or dissolution under the Insolvency,
-- src:1399 | Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, or under the
-- src:1400 | Companies Act 1967* as in force immediately before
-- src:1402 | 30 July 2020 —
-- src:1404 | (i) that are international and commercial in nature; and
-- src:1406 | (ii) that satisfy such conditions as the Rules of Court
-- src:1407 | may prescribe.
@ref s 18D(2)(c) (src:1391-1407)
GIVEN `the proceedings relate to corporate insolvency, restructuring or dissolution under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or the Companies Act 1967 as in force immediately before 30 July 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the proceedings relate to corporate insolvency, restructuring or dissolution under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, or under the Companies Act 1967 as in force immediately before 30 July 2020?
      `the proceedings are international and commercial in nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings international and commercial in nature?
      `the proceedings satisfy the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the proceedings satisfy the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(2)(c) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the corporate insolvency, restructuring or dissolution proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings relate to corporate insolvency, restructuring or dissolution under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or the Companies Act 1967 as in force immediately before 30 July 2020`
           AND `the proceedings are international and commercial in nature`
           AND `the proceedings satisfy the conditions the Rules of Court prescribe` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting subsection (1)": other routes remain

-- s 18D(2)(c), the vintage of the Companies Act 1967: the version "as in force immediately before 30 July 2020" is the version in force on any date before that day (the core holds 30 July 2020).
@ref s 18D(2)(c) the Companies Act 1967 as in force immediately before 30 July 2020 (src:1399-1402)
GIVEN `a date on which the version of the Companies Act 1967 relied on was in force` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the version of the Companies Act 1967 you rely on in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(2)(c) the version of the Companies Act 1967 is one in force before 30 July 2020` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a date on which the version of the Companies Act 1967 relied on was in force` LESS THAN `the day before which the Companies Act 1967 is read under s 18D(2)(c)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Companies Act 1967 as in force immediately before 30 July 2020"

-- s 18D(3). Where the SICC has and exercises jurisdiction under (1) over an action, that jurisdiction includes the four things below. The gate "Where ... has and exercises" is read as a "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05):
-- each answer is JUST FALSE when it is not met.
-- src:1415 | (3) Where the Singapore International Commercial Court has and
-- src:1416 | exercises jurisdiction under subsection (1) in respect of any action,
-- src:1417 | such jurisdiction includes —
@ref s 18D(3) (opening words) (src:1415-1417)
GIVEN `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Singapore International Commercial Court have, and exercise, jurisdiction over the action under section 18D(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(3) the jurisdiction under section 18D(1) includes the further jurisdiction in this subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under subsection (1) in respect of any action"

-- src:1419 | (a) the jurisdiction to hear and try the action upon the joinder
-- src:1420 | of any additional party, if the action continues to maintain
-- src:1421 | an international and commercial character, even if the
-- src:1422 | claim by or against the additional party is not international
-- src:1423 | and commercial in nature;
@ref s 18D(3)(a) (src:1419-1423)
GIVEN `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action continues to maintain an international and commercial character after the joinder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the joinder of the additional party, does the action continue to maintain an international and commercial character?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(3)(a) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the action upon the joinder of an additional party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 18D(3) the jurisdiction under section 18D(1) includes the further jurisdiction in this subsection` `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under subsection (1)"
        IF `the action continues to maintain an international and commercial character after the joinder` THEN JUST TRUE -- the claim by or against the additional party need not itself be international and commercial
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the action continues to maintain an international and commercial character"

-- src:1425 | (b) the jurisdiction to hear and try a counterclaim brought in,
-- src:1426 | and that remains part of, that action, if the action and
-- src:1427 | counterclaim taken as a whole maintain an international
-- src:1428 | and commercial character, even if the counterclaim is not
-- src:1429 | international and commercial in nature;
@ref s 18D(3)(b) (src:1425-1429)
GIVEN `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the counterclaim was brought in, and remains part of, that action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the counterclaim brought in, and does it remain part of, the action?
      `the action and counterclaim taken as a whole maintain an international and commercial character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Taken as a whole, do the action and the counterclaim maintain an international and commercial character?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(3)(b) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the counterclaim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 18D(3) the jurisdiction under section 18D(1) includes the further jurisdiction in this subsection` `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under subsection (1)"
        IF `the counterclaim was brought in, and remains part of, that action` AND `the action and counterclaim taken as a whole maintain an international and commercial character` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the action and counterclaim taken as a whole maintain an international and commercial character"

-- s 18D(3)(c). Third party proceedings: brought by a defendant or respondent against a party not already a party to the action, if (i) the Rules' requirements for third party proceedings are met and
-- (ii) the main action and the third party proceedings taken as a whole maintain an international and commercial character. The two defined terms of the paragraph are the proceedings and the party.
