      `the requirements the Rules of Court prescribe for third party proceedings are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements the Rules of Court prescribe for the bringing of third party proceedings satisfied?
      `the main action and the third party proceedings taken as a whole maintain an international and commercial character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Taken as a whole, do the main action and the third party proceedings maintain an international and commercial character?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(3)(c) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the third party proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 18D(3) the jurisdiction under section 18D(1) includes the further jurisdiction in this subsection` `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under subsection (1)"
        IF NOT `the proceedings are brought by a defendant or respondent against a party who is not already a party to the action` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings (called ... third party proceedings) brought by a defendant or respondent against any party ... who is not already a party to the action"
        IF `the requirements the Rules of Court prescribe for third party proceedings are satisfied` AND `the main action and the third party proceedings taken as a whole maintain an international and commercial character` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (i) the requirements ... are satisfied; and (ii) the main action and the third party proceedings taken as a whole maintain an international and commercial character"

-- s 18D(3)(d). Subsequent party proceedings: brought by a third party against a party not already a party to the third party proceedings, if (i) the Rules' requirements for subsequent party proceedings are met and
