-- s 18D(4). (3)(d) applies, with the appropriate modifications, to proceedings brought by a subsequent party against a party not already a party to the subsequent party proceedings, as if the subsequent party were a third party
-- and the subsequent party proceedings were third party proceedings. The modification is the same rule applied one step on: this calls (3)(d)'s own function.
-- src:1471 | (4) Subsection (3)(d) applies, with the appropriate modifications, to
-- src:1472 | any proceedings brought by a subsequent party against any party who
-- src:1473 | is not already a party to the subsequent party proceedings, as if the
-- src:1474 | subsequent party were a third party, and the subsequent party
-- src:1475 | proceedings were third party proceedings.
@ref s 18D(4) (src:1471-1475)
GIVEN `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are brought by a subsequent party against a party who is not already a party to the subsequent party proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings brought by a subsequent party against someone who is not already a party to the subsequent party proceedings?
      `the requirements the Rules of Court prescribe are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements the Rules of Court prescribe for the bringing of these proceedings satisfied?
      `the proceedings taken together with the earlier proceedings as a whole maintain an international and commercial character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Taken as a whole with the earlier proceedings in the action, do these proceedings maintain an international and commercial character?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18D(4) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the proceedings brought by a subsequent party` MEANS
    `s 18D(3)(d) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the subsequent party proceedings`
        `the Singapore International Commercial Court has and exercises jurisdiction under section 18D(1) over the action`
        `the proceedings are brought by a subsequent party against a party who is not already a party to the subsequent party proceedings`
        `the requirements the Rules of Court prescribe are satisfied`
        `the proceedings taken together with the earlier proceedings as a whole maintain an international and commercial character`

§§§ `Section 18F: Effect of jurisdiction agreement`

-- The three things s 18F(1) says the parties are considered to have agreed.
DECLARE `s 18F(1) agreed term` IS ONE OF
    `s 18F(1)(a) to submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court`
    `s 18F(1)(b) to carry out any judgment or order of the Singapore International Commercial Court without undue delay`
    `s 18F(1)(c) to waive any recourse to a court or tribunal outside Singapore against any judgment or order, and against its enforcement, insofar as the recourse can be validly waived`

-- s 18F(1), (2). Plain gloss: are parties to an agreement to submit to the SICC's jurisdiction considered to have agreed to this term? (2): (1)(a), (b), (c) apply ONLY if there is no express provision to the contrary
-- in the agreement. (c) goes as far as the recourse can validly be waived.
-- src:1483 | 18F.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), the parties to an agreement to
-- src:1484 | submit to the jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial
-- src:1485 | Court are considered to have agreed —
-- src:1487 | (a) to submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Singapore
-- src:1488 | International Commercial Court;
-- src:1490 | (b) to carry out any judgment or order of the Singapore
-- src:1491 | International Commercial Court without undue delay; and
-- src:1493 | (c) to waive any recourse to any court or tribunal outside
-- src:1494 | Singapore against any judgment or order of the Singapore
-- src:1495 | International Commercial Court, and against the
-- src:1502 | enforcement of the judgment or order, insofar as the
-- src:1503 | recourse can be validly waived.
-- src:1507 | (2) Subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c) applies only if there is no express
-- src:1508 | provision to the contrary in the agreement.
@ref s 18F(1), (2) (src:1483-1508)
GIVEN term IS A `s 18F(1) agreed term` @desc Which term: (a) submitting to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court; (b) carrying out its judgments and orders without undue delay; (c) waiving recourse to any court or tribunal outside Singapore?
      `there is an agreement to submit to the jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement between the parties to submit to the jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court?
      `the agreement has an express provision to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement have an express provision to the contrary?
      `the recourse can be validly waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For waiver of recourse outside Singapore: can the recourse be validly waived?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is an agreement to submit to the jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the parties to an agreement to submit to the jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court"
        IF `the agreement has an express provision to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies only if there is no express provision to the contrary in the agreement"
        IF term EQUALS `s 18F(1)(c) to waive any recourse to a court or tribunal outside Singapore against any judgment or order, and against its enforcement, insofar as the recourse can be validly waived`
           AND NOT `the recourse can be validly waived` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "insofar as the recourse can be validly waived"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§§ `Sections 18G and 18H: Composition of the Singapore International Commercial Court`

-- s 18G. Every proceeding in the SICC is heard and disposed of before a single Judge or 3 Judges. A number outside the two named answers NOTHING (a bare "is to be", question QB; fork F7): the text names no "only" and no consequence.
-- src:1514 | 18G. Every proceeding in the Singapore International Commercial
-- src:1515 | Court is to be heard and disposed of before a single Judge or 3 Judges.
@ref s 18G (src:1514-1515)
GIVEN `the number of Judges` IS A NUMBER @desc Before how many Judges is the proceeding to be heard and disposed of?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18G the proceeding is to be heard and disposed of before this number of Judges, as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of Judges` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the number of Judges` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is to be heard and disposed of before a single Judge or 3 Judges" names two numbers with no "only" and states what is to be done, not what follows if it is not (fork F7)

-- s 18H(1). Section 18H applies where a case in the SICC is heard before 3 Judges. A "where" not met is a no for the section.
-- src:1522 | 18H.—(1) This section applies where a case in the Singapore
-- src:1523 | International Commercial Court is heard before 3 Judges.
@ref s 18H(1) (src:1522-1523)
GIVEN `the number of Judges before whom the case is heard` IS A NUMBER @desc Before how many Judges is the case in the Singapore International Commercial Court heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18H(1) section 18H applies to the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of Judges before whom the case is heard` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a case in the Singapore International Commercial Court is heard before 3 Judges"

-- s 18H(2). The Chief Justice appoints one of the Judges to preside.
-- src:1527 | (2) The Chief Justice is to appoint one of the Judges to preside.
@ref s 18H(2) (src:1527)
GIVEN `the case is heard before 3 Judges` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Judge who presides was appointed to preside by the Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Judge who presides appointed to preside by the Chief Justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18H(2) the presiding Judge was appointed by the Chief Justice, as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the case is heard before 3 Judges` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a case ... is heard before 3 Judges"
        IF `the Judge who presides was appointed to preside by the Chief Justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The Chief Justice is to appoint one of the Judges to preside" states a duty and does not say what follows if the Judge who presides was not so appointed (fork F7)

-- How a case before 3 Judges is decided under s 18H(3).
DECLARE `s 18H(3) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, counterclaim or application`
    `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against it`
    `s 18H(3) not covered`

-- s 18H(3). The case is decided in accordance with the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing it. Without a majority (no Judge, or an even division) the Act does not say.
-- src:1531 | (3) The case is to be decided in accordance with the opinion of the
-- src:1532 | majority of the Judges hearing the case.
@ref s 18H(3) (src:1531-1532)
GIVEN split IS A `Split of opinion`
GIVETH A `s 18H(3) decision`
`s 18H(3) how the case is decided` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF split's `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` GREATER THAN split's `Judges against it` THEN `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, counterclaim or application`
        IF split's `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` LESS THAN split's `Judges against it` THEN `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against it`
        OTHERWISE `s 18H(3) not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no majority

-- s 18H(4) and (5). A case is to be reheard if one or more of the Judges are unable to continue hearing it for any reason, subject to (5); where ONE Judge is unable, the remaining 2 may continue to hear and
-- determine the case if the parties consent. Whether the remaining 2 do continue is theirs: with one Judge unable and the parties consenting, the Act leaves rehearing or continuing open (NOTHING).
-- src:1536 | (4) Subject to subsection (5), a case is to be reheard if one or more
-- src:1537 | of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case for any reason.
-- src:1541 | (5) Where one Judge is unable to continue hearing a case for any
-- src:1542 | reason, the remaining 2 Judges may continue to hear and determine
-- src:1543 | the case if the parties consent.
@ref s 18H(4), (5) (src:1536-1543)
GIVEN `how many of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case, for any reason?
      `the parties consent to the remaining 2 Judges continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the parties consent to the remaining 2 Judges continuing to hear and determine the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18H(4) the case is to be reheard` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how many of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case` LESS THAN 1 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if one or more of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case"
        IF `how many of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case` EQUALS 1 AND `the parties consent to the remaining 2 Judges continuing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (5)": the remaining 2 "may continue"; the Act does not say whether they do
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 18H(5) (src:1541-1543)
GIVEN `how many of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case` IS A NUMBER
      `the parties consent to the remaining 2 Judges continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18H(5) the remaining 2 Judges may continue to hear and determine the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`how many of the Judges are unable to continue hearing the case` EQUALS 1) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where one Judge is unable to continue hearing a case for any reason"
        IF `the parties consent to the remaining 2 Judges continuing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the parties consent"

-- How a case heard by 2 Judges under s 18H(5) is determined (s 18H(6)).
DECLARE `s 18H(6) outcome` IS ONE OF
    `s 18H(6)(a) determined according to the opinion the 2 Judges share`
    `s 18H(6)(b) the claim, counterclaim or application is dismissed`
    `s 18H(6) not covered`

-- s 18H(6), the yes/no twin of the determination below: does the subsection apply to this case? "Where a case is heard by 2 Judges under subsection (5)": a "where" not met is a no for the subsection.
-- src:1547 | (6) Where a case is heard by 2 Judges under subsection (5) —
@ref s 18H(6) (opening words) (src:1547)
GIVEN `the case is heard by 2 Judges under section 18H(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case heard by 2 Judges under section 18H(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18H(6) this subsection applies to the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the case is heard by 2 Judges under section 18H(5)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a case is heard by 2 Judges under subsection (5)"

-- s 18H(6). Where a case is heard by 2 Judges under (5): (a) the same opinion: determined according to it; (b) different opinions on any claim, counterclaim or application: that claim, counterclaim or application is dismissed.
-- src:1547 | (6) Where a case is heard by 2 Judges under subsection (5) —
-- src:1549 | (a) if the 2 Judges have the same opinion, the case is to be
-- src:1550 | determined according to their opinion; or
-- src:1552 | (b) if the 2 Judges have different opinions on any claim,
-- src:1553 | counterclaim or application, the claim, counterclaim or
-- src:1554 | application (as the case may be) is to be dismissed.
@ref s 18H(6) (src:1547-1554)
GIVEN split IS A `Split of opinion`
GIVETH A `s 18H(6) outcome`
`s 18H(6) how the case heard by 2 Judges is determined` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT ((split's `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` PLUS split's `Judges against it`) EQUALS 2) THEN `s 18H(6) not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a case is heard by 2 Judges under subsection (5)"
        IF split's `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` EQUALS 1 THEN `s 18H(6)(b) the claim, counterclaim or application is dismissed`
        OTHERWISE `s 18H(6)(a) determined according to the opinion the 2 Judges share`

§§§ `Section 18I: Powers of Singapore International Commercial Court, generally`

-- s 18I(1). Plain gloss: may the SICC exercise this power? Such powers as the General Division may exercise in its original civil jurisdiction, EXCEPT (a) the power under paragraph 1 of the First Schedule
-- (seam 2: the First Schedule, scja3, answers it) and (b) any power that must be exercised through the Family Division of the High Court.
-- src:1566 | 18I.—(1) The Singapore International Commercial Court may
-- src:1567 | exercise such powers as the General Division may exercise in its
-- src:1568 | original civil jurisdiction, except —
-- src:1570 | (a) the power under paragraph 1 of the First Schedule; and
-- src:1572 | (b) any power that must be exercised through the Family
-- src:1573 | Division of the High Court.
@ref s 18I(1) (src:1566-1573)
GIVEN `the General Division may exercise the power in its original civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a power the General Division may exercise in its original civil jurisdiction?
      `sch 1 para 1 the power is the power under paragraph 1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the power must be exercised through the Family Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a power that must be exercised through the Family Division of the High Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18I(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may exercise the power` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sch 1 para 1 the power is the power under paragraph 1` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except (a) the power under paragraph 1 of the First Schedule"
        IF `the power must be exercised through the Family Division of the High Court` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... (b) any power that must be exercised through the Family Division of the High Court"
        IF NOT `the General Division may exercise the power in its original civil jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such powers as the General Division may exercise in its original civil jurisdiction"
        IF `sch 1 para 1 the power is the power under paragraph 1` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the power is the one in paragraph 1 of the First Schedule is not given
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 18I(2). The SICC exercises its powers in accordance with the Rules of Court and any other written law relating to that Court or those powers. A bare "is to" not met answers NOTHING (QB; F7).
-- src:1577 | (2) The Singapore International Commercial Court is to exercise its
-- src:1578 | powers in accordance with the Rules of Court, and any other written
-- src:1579 | law, relating to that Court or those powers.
@ref s 18I(2) (src:1577-1579)
GIVEN `the power is exercised in accordance with the Rules of Court and any other written law relating to that Court or the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power exercised in accordance with the Rules of Court and any other written law relating to the Singapore International Commercial Court or the power?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18I(2) the Singapore International Commercial Court exercises the power as the Act requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the power is exercised in accordance with the Rules of Court and any other written law relating to that Court or the power` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to exercise its powers in accordance with the Rules of Court, and any other written law" states a duty and does not say what follows if it is not done (fork F7)

§§§ `Section 18J: Transfer of cases`

-- s 18J(4). In s 18J, "General Division" does not include the SICC (fork K1: the other sections count it).
-- src:1610 | (4) In this section, “General Division” does not include the
-- src:1611 | Singapore International Commercial Court.
@ref s 18J(4) (src:1610-1611)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18J(4) the court is the General Division for the purposes of section 18J` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, “General Division” does not include the Singapore International Commercial Court"
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 18J(4) says only that the Singapore International Commercial Court is not included

-- s 18J(1). The SICC may transfer a case commenced in that Court to the General Division in accordance with the Rules of Court.
-- src:1585 | 18J.—(1) The Singapore International Commercial Court may
-- src:1586 | transfer a case commenced in that Court to the General Division in
-- src:1587 | accordance with the Rules of Court.
@ref s 18J(1) (src:1585-1587)
GIVEN `the case was commenced in the Singapore International Commercial Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the case commenced in the Singapore International Commercial Court?
      `the transfer is in accordance with the Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer in accordance with the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18J(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may transfer the case to the General Division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the case was commenced in the Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a case commenced in that Court"
        IF `the transfer is in accordance with the Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with the Rules of Court"

-- s 18J(2). The General Division may transfer a case commenced in the General Division to the SICC in accordance with the Rules of Court.
-- src:1591 | (2) The General Division may transfer a case commenced in the
-- src:1592 | General Division to the Singapore International Commercial Court in
-- src:1593 | accordance with the Rules of Court.
@ref s 18J(2) (src:1591-1593)
GIVEN `the case was commenced in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the case commenced in the General Division?
      `the transfer is in accordance with the Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18J(2) the General Division may transfer the case to the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the case was commenced in the General Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a case commenced in the General Division"
        IF `the transfer is in accordance with the Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with the Rules of Court"

-- s 18J(3). Where a case is transferred under (1) or (2): (a) the receiving court may permit a matter already adduced to remain in evidence, though different rules of evidence apply there;
-- (b) the transferring court and the receiving court may make any consequential order in accordance with the Rules of Court.
-- src:1597 | (3) Where a case is transferred under subsection (1) or (2) —
-- src:1599 | (a) the court to which the case is transferred may permit any
-- src:1600 | matter that has been adduced to remain in evidence, even
-- src:1601 | though different rules of evidence may apply in the court to
-- src:1602 | which the case is transferred; and
-- src:1604 | (b) the court transferring the case and the court to which the
-- src:1605 | case is transferred may make any consequential order in
-- src:1606 | accordance with the Rules of Court.
@ref s 18J(3) (src:1597-1606)
GIVEN `the case is transferred under section 18J(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case transferred under section 18J(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18J(3)(a) the court to which the case is transferred may permit a matter that has been adduced to remain in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the case is transferred under section 18J(1) or (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a case is transferred under subsection (1) or (2)"

@ref s 18J(3)(b) (src:1604-1606)
GIVEN `the case is transferred under section 18J(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made in accordance with the Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consequential order made in accordance with the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18J(3)(b) the courts may make the consequential order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the case is transferred under section 18J(1) or (2)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a case is transferred under subsection (1) or (2)"
        IF `the order is made in accordance with the Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with the Rules of Court"

§§§ `Sections 18K and 18L: Rules of evidence; foreign law`

-- s 18K(1)(a), (b). Plain gloss: in this case, is the SICC not bound to apply a rule of evidence under Singapore law, and may it apply other rules? Only in the cases and to the extent the Rules of Court provide.
-- src:1622 | 18K.—(1) The Singapore International Commercial Court —
-- src:1624 | (a) is not bound to apply any rule of evidence under Singapore
-- src:1625 | law in such cases and to such extent as the Rules of Court
-- src:1626 | may provide; and
-- src:1628 | (b) may, in those cases, apply other rules of evidence (whether
-- src:1629 | such rules are found under any foreign law or otherwise) in
-- src:1630 | accordance with the Rules of Court.
@ref s 18K(1) (src:1622-1630)
GIVEN `the Rules of Court provide that the Singapore International Commercial Court need not apply a Singapore rule of evidence in this case and to this extent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Rules of Court provide that, in this case and to this extent, the Singapore International Commercial Court is not bound to apply a rule of evidence under Singapore law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18K(1)(a) the Singapore International Commercial Court is not bound to apply the rule of evidence under Singapore law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Rules of Court provide that the Singapore International Commercial Court need not apply a Singapore rule of evidence in this case and to this extent` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in such cases and to such extent as the Rules of Court may provide"

@ref s 18K(1)(b) (src:1628-1630)
GIVEN `the Rules of Court allow other rules of evidence to be applied in this case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Rules of Court allow the Singapore International Commercial Court to apply other rules of evidence (under foreign law or otherwise) in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18K(1)(b) the Singapore International Commercial Court may apply other rules of evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Rules of Court allow other rules of evidence to be applied in this case` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in those cases ... in accordance with the Rules of Court"

-- s 18K(2). In s 18K(1), "rule of evidence" includes any rule of law relating to privilege, or to the taking of evidence.
-- src:1634 | (2) In subsection (1), “rule of evidence” includes any rule of law
-- src:1635 | relating to privilege, or to the taking of evidence.
@ref s 18K(2) (src:1634-1635)
GIVEN `it is a rule of evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a rule of evidence?
      `it is a rule of law relating to privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a rule of law relating to privilege?
      `it is a rule of law relating to the taking of evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a rule of law relating to the taking of evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18K(2) the rule is a rule of evidence for the purposes of section 18K(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a rule of law relating to privilege` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a rule of law relating to the taking of evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a rule of evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“rule of evidence” includes any rule of law relating to privilege, or to the taking of evidence"

-- s 18L(1), (2). In the cases the Rules of Court prescribe, the SICC may order a question of foreign law determined on submissions instead of proof; in doing so it may have regard to the matters the Rules prescribe.
-- src:1641 | 18L.—(1) The Singapore International Commercial Court may, in
-- src:1642 | such cases as the Rules of Court may prescribe, order that any
-- src:1643 | question of foreign law be determined on the basis of submissions
-- src:1644 | instead of proof.
-- src:1648 | (2) In determining any question of foreign law on the basis of
-- src:1649 | submissions, the Singapore International Commercial Court may
-- src:1650 | have regard to such matters as the Rules of Court may prescribe.
@ref s 18L (src:1641-1650)
GIVEN `the Rules of Court prescribe the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Rules of Court prescribe this kind of case as one where a question of foreign law may be determined on submissions instead of proof?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18L(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may order the question of foreign law determined on the basis of submissions instead of proof` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Rules of Court prescribe the case` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in such cases as the Rules of Court may prescribe"

@ref s 18L(2) (src:1648-1650)
GIVEN `the matter is one the Rules of Court prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court prescribe for the Singapore International Commercial Court to have regard to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18L(2) the Singapore International Commercial Court may have regard to the matter in determining foreign law on submissions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is one the Rules of Court prescribe` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such matters as the Rules of Court may prescribe"

§§§ `Section 18M: Representation by foreign lawyers and law experts`

-- s 18M. Plain gloss: may a party to a case in the SICC, or to an appeal from it, be represented by this foreign lawyer or law expert? In accordance with the Rules of Court, and if registered in accordance with
-- Part 4B of the Legal Profession Act 1966. The grant names its complement, so anyone else is outside it (NOTHING).
-- src:1656 | 18M. A party to a case in the Singapore International Commercial
-- src:1657 | Court, or to an appeal from that Court, may in accordance with the
-- src:1658 | Rules of Court be represented by a foreign lawyer or law expert who
-- src:1659 | is registered in accordance with Part 4B of the Legal Profession
-- src:1660 | Act 1966.
@ref s 18M (src:1656-1660)
GIVEN `the party is a party to a case in the Singapore International Commercial Court or to an appeal from that Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to a case in the Singapore International Commercial Court, or to an appeal from that Court?
      `the representative is a foreign lawyer or law expert registered in accordance with Part 4B of the Legal Profession Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a foreign lawyer or law expert registered in accordance with Part 4B of the Legal Profession Act 1966?
      `the representation is in accordance with the Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the representation in accordance with the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18M the party may be represented by the foreign lawyer or law expert` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the party is a party to a case in the Singapore International Commercial Court or to an appeal from that Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party to a case in the Singapore International Commercial Court, or to an appeal from that Court"
        IF NOT `the representative is a foreign lawyer or law expert registered in accordance with Part 4B of the Legal Profession Act 1966` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a foreign lawyer or law expert who is registered in accordance with Part 4B of the Legal Profession Act 1966"
        IF `the representation is in accordance with the Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may in accordance with the Rules of Court be represented"
